WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.570
The real fit starts with zero weights and
the training target mean as its intercept.

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:06.747
All eight thousand,

00:00:06.747 --> 00:00:11.657
six hundred and forty five rows initially
receive one hundred and forty three point

00:00:11.657 --> 00:00:13.110
seven nine rentals.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:14.750
For record fifty four,

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:19.730
that is below the observed one hundred
and fifty four by about ten point two one.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:25.660
The initial bias gradient is nearly zero
because the residuals sum to zero at the

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:26.370
training mean.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.570
That does not make each row correct.

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:32.550
Calendar weights can still explain
the differences around that average.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:36.960
The initialization gives us a direct
connection from the earlier constant

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:39.750
baseline to learned calendar adjustments.

00:00:42.283 --> 00:00:47.447
The first standardized hour eight gradient
is about negative twenty four point nine

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:47.973
six.

00:00:48.743 --> 00:00:53.823
Multiplying by rate zero point one and
subtracting gives a positive weight near

00:00:53.823 --> 00:00:55.133
two point five zero.

00:00:56.123 --> 00:01:00.173
January has a positive gradient
near twenty five point nine six,

00:01:00.523 --> 00:01:02.113
so its weight becomes negative.

00:01:02.923 --> 00:01:04.893
The whole batch determines
these directions.

00:01:06.183 --> 00:01:10.420
The full vector forecast for record fifty
four moves to one hundred and forty seven

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:12.973
point zero four after one update,

00:01:13.443 --> 00:01:16.493
then one hundred and forty nine
point nine three after two.

00:01:17.283 --> 00:01:20.013
A separate scalar
calculation reproduces both.

00:01:20.523 --> 00:01:24.723
We must calculate the whole vector
forecast because centering makes

00:01:24.723 --> 00:01:28.113
originally inactive
columns contribute too.

00:01:29.815 --> 00:01:34.475
Each iteration predicts every training
row and averages its loss and gradient

00:01:34.475 --> 00:01:35.265
contributions.

00:01:36.255 --> 00:01:39.065
The norm combines weight
and intercept gradients.

00:01:39.775 --> 00:01:43.625
The fit stops when that norm
is at most one ten millionth.

00:01:44.155 --> 00:01:46.685
The maximum budget is
ten thousand updates.

00:01:47.215 --> 00:01:52.465
History includes the initial state as
step zero, followed by each actual update.

00:01:53.195 --> 00:01:55.875
This run converges after
two hundred updates,

00:01:55.875 --> 00:02:01.355
with a norm near nine point seven
two times ten to the negative eight.

00:02:01.355 --> 00:02:05.165
If the budget expired first,
the record would say unconverged.

00:02:05.875 --> 00:02:10.085
Validation is loaded only after fitting
and the independent reference solve.

00:02:10.795 --> 00:02:13.925
Its answers do not select
the scaler or stopping point.

00:02:15.942 --> 00:02:20.222
The final forecast for our training hour
is one hundred and seventy four point

00:02:20.222 --> 00:02:21.072
seven eight.

00:02:21.622 --> 00:02:24.372
It is now above its target of
one hundred and fifty four.

00:02:25.082 --> 00:02:28.518
Yet the full training objective
fell from about eight thousand,

00:02:28.518 --> 00:02:32.172
nine hundred and fifty to three thousand,
one hundred and sixty eight.

00:02:32.622 --> 00:02:36.392
Why did this hour become
worse after the early updates?

00:02:36.842 --> 00:02:40.532
Each calendar coefficient
is shared across many hours.

00:02:41.022 --> 00:02:45.082
A change can help enough other rows to
lower their combined objective while

00:02:45.082 --> 00:02:46.272
hurting this one.

00:02:47.002 --> 00:02:51.402
Full batch optimization does not promise
a steadily shrinking error for every

00:02:51.402 --> 00:02:52.332
observation.

00:02:52.962 --> 00:02:55.372
The single hour helps
us read the calculation;

00:02:56.202 --> 00:02:58.552
all training rows determine
the fitted compromise.

00:03:00.942 --> 00:03:04.812
A training only curvature check
guards the fixed step size.

00:03:05.282 --> 00:03:09.962
Append the intercept column and calculate
the largest eigenvalue of the averaged

00:03:09.962 --> 00:03:11.612
design Gram matrix.

00:03:12.062 --> 00:03:13.972
For this quadratic objective,

00:03:14.102 --> 00:03:19.262
a positive rate below two divided by that
curvature contracts positive curvature

00:03:19.262 --> 00:03:19.872
directions.

00:03:20.342 --> 00:03:22.952
The limit is about zero point nine four,

00:03:23.342 --> 00:03:25.692
so zero point one is inside it.

00:03:26.262 --> 00:03:29.552
Safety does not say how quickly
the tolerance will be reached.

00:03:29.922 --> 00:03:32.212
We measure that separately
through saved history.

00:03:33.342 --> 00:03:37.242
Changing validation outcomes in a fixture
leaves the model and stopping record

00:03:37.242 --> 00:03:40.312
unchanged while the
evaluation score changes.

00:03:40.902 --> 00:03:43.592
This is one checked full batch reference.

00:03:44.182 --> 00:03:47.092
Optimizer and schedule
comparisons remain later work.

